<summary>Optional sections</summary>

**Dependencies & risks**
- Base libraries (OAuth-front framework + Drive tool layer) to be **chosen during build**, not pre-decided. Candidates surfaced in research include FastMCP (OAuth-front) and existing open-source Google Drive MCP servers with Shared-Drive + service-account support; the coding agent should evaluate and select against the requirements above rather than treat any as given.
- **Key-man risk:** single-maintainer internal tool; document setup and secrets location in the IT runbook.
- **Platform risk:** claude.ai custom-connector OAuth has had breakage (Dec 2025 regression); pin behavior with a post-deploy smoke test.

**Rollout & rollback**
- Roll out to a single test user first (verify FR2–FR5), then enable org-wide.
- Rollback = Owner disables the connector in claude.ai; no data migration involved.

**Later PRDs (roadmap, not v1 scope)**
- **PRD 2:** write/edit operations (incl. rich Google Docs editing via structured batchUpdate) and higher read fidelity (Sheet formulas, Slide structure).
- **PRD 3:** monitoring — usage analytics, dashboards, alerting on the audit log.

**Open questions**
